 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Sign in Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a sign in form?\", \"a\": \"A sign in form records who arrived at a place and when. Most versions also ask who the person came to see and record when they leave. Kept together, those entries become a log of every visit to the building.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a sign in form?\", \"a\": \"Decide what each entry must capture: a name, the time in, the time out, and one field that fits the place, such as the host or the work area. Describe that to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, and it builds the form plus a table that stores every visit. Then set the form on a tablet at the entrance.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I sign in an online form?\", \"a\": \"Open the form on the tablet at the entrance, or follow the link your host sent. Fill in your name and the other fields, then tap the sign-in button. On the way out, find your name on the same form and sign out.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a sign in form template to start from?\", \"a\": \"Template sites offer printable sheets with the basic columns. A sign in form template stops fitting once your door has its own rules, like a host to notify or a closing check. Describing the form you need gets you those rules from the first version.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make a free sign in form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing a free sign in form, and responses have no cap. When people need to claim a slot before they arrive, build a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/sign-up-form'>sign up form</a> instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a digital sign in sheet work?\", \"a\": \"A digital sign in sheet runs on a tablet or a phone instead of a clipboard. Each entry is saved with a time stamp, and signing out closes the visit. A second entrance needs only a second tablet showing the same form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a digital sign in sheet better than paper?\", \"a\": \"For a busy door, usually yes. A digital sign in sheet stamps the time on its own and keeps earlier names out of the next visitor's view. It also totals each person's hours without anyone retyping a page. Paper still has a job as the backup. Keep a printed sign in form PDF at the desk for the morning the tablet will not turn on.\"}, {\"q\": \"What app can I use for a sign in form?\", \"a\": \"Any forms app that opens in a tablet browser can take a name and an arrival time. The differences show up after that, in signing visitors out and telling a host that someone is waiting. Emergent builds a sign in form with both steps attached and keeps the visit log in your own database.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I put a sign in form online?\", \"a\": \"Publish the form, then open its link on a tablet at your entrance. Post the same link by the door for anyone who prefers their own phone. Gyms and climbing walls often have guests sign a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/liability-waiver-form'>liability waiver form</a> during the same visit.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are sign in forms used for?\", \"a\": \"Sign in forms keep a record of who was in a building and for how long. Warehouses log contractors with them, and schools use them for parents who pick a child up early. Programs that also need a contact for each volunteer pair one with an emergency contact form.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}